[{:db/id -1
 :adr/id "adr-2609071900-a-governed-artifact-that-hashes-three-of-its-inputs"
 :adr/title "The governed release artifact asserts over three inputs and is compiled from a dozen"
 :adr/status "accepted"
 :adr/date "2026-09-07"
 :adr/body "## Context\n\n`network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api` is the Worker behind `api.murakumo.cloud`. It\ndoes not build at deploy time. `scripts/package-release.mjs` unpacks a\n**committed** artifact (`release/cljs/worker.js.gz`, `ui.js.gz`,\n`ui-manifest.edn.gz`) into `dist/` and `public/js/`, after asserting that each\narchive matches the digests in `release/cljs/manifest.json` and that a\n`sourceDigest()` over the repository still equals the manifest's. `npm run\ndeploy` runs it before `wrangler deploy`, so a mismatch blocks the deploy.\n\nThe intent is reproducibility: the shipped bytes are tied to a recorded source\nstate, and a change to source fails closed until the artifact is refreshed.\n\n## What was measured, 2026-09-07\n\n**The digest covers three inputs. The build has many more.**\n\n`sourceDigest()` hashes `deps.edn`, `shadow-cljs.edn`, and this repository's\n`src/**/*.clj[cs]`. But `deps.edn` puts two external source trees directly on\n`:paths` --- `../../kotoba-lang/treasury/src` and `../cloud-murakumo/src` ---\nand declares roughly ten `:local/root` sibling libraries (`kotobase-peer`,\n`html`, `css`, `treasury`, `org-chainagnostic-cacao`, `murakumo`, `sekisho`,\n`org-ietf-ed25519`, ...). Their `.cljc` compiles into `worker.js`. None of it is\nhashed. A sibling can move while the digest is byte-identical, and\n`package-release.mjs` still prints `ok:true`.\n\n**The artifact does not reproduce from its own recorded state.** Checking out\nthe commit that last refreshed `manifest.json`, in a clean clone, with every\nsibling checkout verified unchanged and `.shadow-cljs` cleared, and rebuilding\nwith shadow-cljs 2.28.20:\n\n```\ncommitted  1,142,830 bytes  sha256 d60a0b0c...   (== manifest outputSha256)\nrebuilt    1,142,816 bytes  sha256 34df8233...\nfirst difference at byte 655:  `oa=`  vs  `na=`\n```\n\nFourteen bytes smaller, and the divergence is global Closure symbol\nreassignment beginning in the goog runtime preamble --- not a local edit\npropagating. Whatever the remaining input is, the digest does not see it.\n\n## Decision\n\n**Do not tighten the digest yet; make the claim honest first.**\n\nWidening `sourceDigest()` to cover the sibling inputs would be the obviously\ncorrect fix, and it is the wrong first move: every sibling commit would then\ninvalidate the artifact and demand a refresh, and *refreshing is exactly what\ndoes not currently work*. Tightening a gate whose remedy is broken converts a\nnarrow guarantee into an undeployable repository.\n\nSo: `package-release.mjs` now states its own scope, in the assertion message\nand in the `ok:true` payload (`proves` / `doesNotProve`), so a reader of a build\nlog learns what the green means without opening the file.\n\n`ok:true` means *this repository's own CLJS inputs have not changed since the\nartifact was built*. It does **not** mean *this artifact is what the source\ncompiles to*.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Touching any `.cljc` in that repository blocks deploys until the artifact is\n  refreshed, and that refresh is currently not attributable. Budget for it.\n  A prose-only fix to `src/` was reverted for exactly this reason\n  (`network-awai/cloud-murakumo-api` `be33822`) rather than shipping a 1.1 MB\n  bundle that could not be tied to the change it was supposed to carry.\n- `scripts/` is outside the digest, which is why this honesty change could land\n  without re-blocking the repository. That asymmetry is worth knowing.\n- The open question is which input differs. Candidates not yet excluded:\n  the shadow-cljs/Closure version that produced the committed artifact, the\n  `node_modules` tree present at build time, and `:local/root` siblings'\n  transitive `:git/sha` dependencies (which move independently of the sibling's\n  own working tree, and were verified unchanged only at the sibling level).\n\n## The shape, beyond this repository\n\nA gate that asserts over a subset of its inputs and reports a single green is\nthe same failure this workspace keeps finding (ADR-2608136000): the check that\ncould not see a change returns what a check that saw no change returns. Here it\nis one step subtler --- the gate is *correct* about what it hashes, and the\nerror is in what a reader takes the green to mean. Naming the scope in the\noutput is cheaper than widening the hash, and it is what makes the eventual\nwidening safe to do.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```bash\ncd <clone of cloud-murakumo-api at the manifest.json commit>\nrm -rf .shadow-cljs\nclojure -Sdeps '{:deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \\\"2.28.20\\\"}}}' \\\n  -M -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release worker\n# compare dist/worker.js against gunzip -c release/cljs/worker.js.gz\n```\n\nDo not carry today's byte counts forward. Run it.\n\n## 改訂 2026-09-07 — この ADR が引用した commit は、引用した内容を持っていなかった\n\n本文は `package-release.mjs` の scope 明示を `be33822` が運んだと書いたが、\nその commit は **revert しか含んでいなかった**。scope の変更は worktree で\nunstaged のまま残り、`git commit` を `-a` 無しで打ったので staged だった revert\nだけが commit された。worktree はその後撤去され、変更は失われた。\n\n実際に運んでいるのは **`b3eaa00`**（42 行、`proves` / `doesNotProve` を含む）。\n`be33822` は revert（deploy 可能性の回復）のみ。\n\n⚠ **形として残す価値があるのはここ。** commit した直後に `git show --stat` を\n見ていれば 1 行で分かった。見なかったので、**landed していないものを根拠として\n引用する ADR** が main に載り、その ADR 自身が「ゲートの green を読み違えるな」と\n論じていた。`ok:true` の意味を読み違えるなと書いた文書が、`commit=0` の意味を\n読み違えている。\n\ncommit の exit code は「何かが commit された」であって「意図したものが commit\nされた」ではない。**書き換えたファイルは commit の後に `--stat` で読み返す。**"}]
